\   /
 \ /
  X		  V1.05 / 30.1.1991
 / \
/   \PRD  is  a  utility designed for doing file transfers via the XPR.libs
with  a  standalone  CLI command or from other programms (BBS, Points).  It
offers ability to set every XPR parameter from the commandline.  Also, XPRD
allows  real  batch  upload  (not  to  be  mixed up with the pretty useless
pattern matching...)

The calling sequence of XPRD is

    XPRD [-options] SEND|RECEIVE [File1 [file2...]]

SEND or RECEIVE (distinguished only by the first letter) design to transfer
operation  to  be  done.   File1  ...   give the files to be send (or to be
received  with non-batch-protocols).  If you leave out filenames, a default
filename of "NAPFSUELZE" will be used (for batch-DL only).

The following options are avaible:


    -l<libname>		XPR-Library to use (default is "xprzmodem.library")

    -o<string>		option string for XProtocolSetup().

    -d<devname>		defines the serial-IO device to be used. Default
			is "serial.device"

    -u<unit>		defines the serial-IO device UNIT to be used.
			Default is "0"

    -b<num>		defines the size of the read buffer. If this 
			is missed out (or 0), the default value from
			the device setup is used

    -x<baud>		defines the speed of the serial device. If this
			is missed out, the default value from the
			device setup is used

    -p<xpos,ypos>	defines the XPRD-window's X and Y position

    -n			no delay after end of transfer

    -f			forces the XPRD-window to be opened on the
			frontmost screen

    -s			forces the serial device to be opened in SHARED
			mode

    -c			activates carrier detect (will be checked on
			every call to xpr_chkabort())

    -i			display version and copyright information

The following XPR-routines are implemented yet:


  fopen,fclose,fread,fwrite,fseek,finfo,ffirst,fnext
  sread,swrite,sflush
  displayupdate,checkabort,unlink

